* Transformation to a new unit cell (NEWCELL)

+ List of nice cells with increasing size
# n = size of the supercell is n times the input cell.
# rmax = radius of the largest sphere that fits in the supercell (bohr).
# niceness = inverse of the cell skewness, higher is nicer, cubic cell = 1
# nops = symmetry operations of the crystal compatible with the supercell lattice;
#        nindep, ndisp = independent atoms and displacements CREATE_DISPLACEMENTS
#        would generate for this supercell
# For each size, over all the sublattices of that size, the NICEST cell; the most
# symmetric one when several tie. MINDISP chooses the nicest with the fewest ndisp.
# newcell transformation = use these parameters in a NEWCELL command to obtain this cell
#n   rmax   niceness  nops nindep ndisp  -- NEWCELL transformation --
